                <pb facs="0278" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.001 Selassie I/335: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-31T13:00:00+01:00">July 31, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 31—9:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>384. The Embassy is reliably informed that the Emperor of Ethiopia contemplates
                    applying through the Ethiopian Consul General in New York for permission to
                    enter the United States.</p>
                <p>Whatever reason may be officially given for this visit, the Embassy understands
                    that the Emperor will endeavor to raise funds.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
